  "turn": 1,
  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "I found TX-0401 in your account ACC-1005. The amount is **EUR 240.00**, and the details are:\n\n- **Date:** 2026-07-20\n- **Merchant:** TechMart Online\n- **Type:** Card payment, outgoing\n- **Status:** Settled\n\nYour account also shows **TX-0402**, a EUR 240.00 card payment to TechMart Online on 2026-07-14. That is six days earlier, with the same amount and merchant. I'm mentioning it only because it matters for one of the reason codes below.\n\nThese are the dispute reason codes Verta supports, and what each one covers:\n\n1. **duplicate_charge:** The same purchase was charged more than once. TX-0401 and TX-0402 could fall under this if both were for one purchase.\n2. **unauthorized_debit:** You did not authorize the payment.\n3. **fraud_card_not_present:** A card-not-present transaction (online or phone) was made fraudulently, for example with your card details but without your involvement.\n4. **goods_not_received:** You paid for goods that were never delivered.\n5. **service_not_rendered:** You paid for a service that was never provided.\n\nWhich of these applies depends on what happened. If you tell me, I can check whether a dispute is eligible before anything is filed. I won't open one without your confirmation.",
